Example rules for a different gridworld (not this one), in priority order:
```
{"condition": "!g1 & y = G1C & x > G1R & !wall", "action": "up"}
{"condition": "toward & !wall & !hazard", "action": "any"}
{"condition": "!wall & !hazard", "action": "any"}
{"condition": "true", "action": "up"}
```
Rule 1 goes straight up to goal 1 when it is in the same column, above the agent. Rule 2 allows every move towards the next goal that neither hits a wall nor enters a hazard; if two moves qualify, either may be taken. Rule 3 allows any safe move where no move goes towards the goal. The last rule is a catch-all default.
